    "answer": {
      "short": "Peta owes \\$1209.50; total tax payable is \\$19 709.50.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Taxable income} &= 84\\,000-(1000+500)\\\\\\text{Taxable income} &= \\$82\\,500\\end{align*}$$\nThe taxable income is in the \\$80 001–\\$180 000 bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess} &= 82\\,500-80\\,000\\\\\\text{Excess} &= \\$2500\\\\\\text{Income tax} &= 17\\,547+0.37\\times2500\\\\\\text{Income tax} &= \\$18\\,472.00\\\\\\text{Medicare levy} &= 0.015\\times82\\,500\\\\\\text{Medicare levy} &= \\$1237.50\\\\\\text{Total tax payable} &= 18\\,472.00+1237.50\\\\\\text{Total tax payable} &= \\$19\\,709.50\\\\\\text{Instalments}-\\text{Total tax payable} &= 18\\,500-19\\,709.50\\\\\\text{Instalments}-\\text{Total tax payable} &= -\\$1209.50\\end{align*}$$\nPeta owes \\$1209.50 because her tax payments are less than her total tax payable.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
